          },
          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Roots of the Conflict</strong><br>\nThe conflict between Israelis and Palestinians has deeply rooted historical origins. One of these roots lies in the time of the British Mandate over Palestine (1920-1948). During this period, the region experienced an increase in Jewish immigration, often supported by the British mandate rulers. The native Arab population felt threatened, leading to tensions.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Balfour Declaration</strong><br>\nAn important event was the Balfour Declaration of 1917, in which the British government expressed its support for the establishment of a \"national home for the Jewish people\" in Palestine. This declaration increased Jewish immigration and laid the groundwork for future conflicts.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Arab Resistance</strong><br>\nDuring the British Mandate, resistance also grew among the Arab population. They rejected Jewish immigration and the pro-Jewish policies of the British. This led to violent clashes and unrest, such as the Arab uprising of 1936-1939.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
