          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Six-Day War</strong><br>\nIn 1967, the Six-Day War occurred between Israel and the surrounding Arab states. Israel captured territories such as the West Bank and the Gaza Strip. These areas remain at the center of the conflict to this day.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Oslo Accords</strong><br>\nIn 1993 and 1995, the Oslo Accords were signed between Israel and the PLO. They provided for a gradual transfer of control over certain areas to the Palestinians. However, the accords did not bring the hoped-for peace, and the conflict continues.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Current Situation</strong><br>\nThe situation in the Israeli-Palestinian conflict remains tense. Clashes occur frequently and the political conditions are complicated. The search for a permanent solution is difficult and depends on many factors.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
